      <td><strong>Geospatial capability</strong></td>
      <td><strong>Why it matters in Nigeria</strong></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Parcel-linked case records</strong></td>
      <td>Keeps land, permit, title, and compliance evidence connected to one location truth.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr fill="mist">
      <td><strong>Spatial-clearance stage</strong></td>
      <td>Makes location review a visible decision gate instead of an informal back-office step.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Location labels and asset references</strong></td>
      <td>Supports the way agencies and operators actually refer to Nigerian sites and corridors.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr fill="mist">
      <td><strong>Geofence-triggered alerts</strong></td>
      <td>Turns field movement and parcel events into actionable workflow signals.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Offline geofence replay</strong></td>
      <td>Preserves site activity when connectivity is weak and reconciles it safely later.</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

